{
  "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
  "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The rule of lenity requires that any penal statute the government seeks to enforce against an individual must clearly and unambiguous apply to him and, as the government acknowledges its brief in this case, this Court has applied the rule of lenity in numerous recent cases involving mandatory sentencing provisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is it time-honored since Granderson? Is that the first time we did it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The 20-year mandatory minimum in Section 841(b)(1)(A) applies only to defendants who have a prior conviction for a, quote, \"felony drug offense.\" Now, a sensible reading of that provision is that a State law misdemeanor simply does not constitute a felony drug offense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Could I -- could I ask you what you think Congress might have been trying to do with the 1994 amendment under -- under your reading?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: May I ask you a question before going on with this line? You say that both the 802(13) definition has to be satisfied and the 44 definition, right? But was 802(13) ever applicable to this situation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is the following true, that if you are right the reason Congress passed this new definition was it wanted to take those handful of States which have felonies as a year, the ones Justice Alito is talking about, and make clear that they are not covered?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Fisher, could I just go back to what you quoted. Are you quoting -- you're quoting a Sentencing Guideline, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: If it's such a vexing problem, why would Congress have incorporated the problem into the definition of \"felony drug offense\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Saharsky",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SAHARSKY: The term \"felony drug offense\" has only the meaning that Congress gave to it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. If I might pick up where Justice Kennedy left off with the rule of lenity, because we don't want this Court to lose sight of the importance of the rule of lenity in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the Court has no further questions, Government submits the judgment below should be affirmed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How many statutes exist like that, my goodness? You want the government to be held in all statutes to a level that is clear enough to satisfy the clear statement --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-11429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bff4323f9bd226702d2367e5307fccfb18ff9e103ce538f44d2079f7372fde6c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bff4323f9bd2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you,\nMr. Fisher. The case is submitted."
    },
